# Module Run — Defects, DOCX, Google Sync

## Rule

Whenever the user asks to **run a module**, **run a spec**, or **execute test cases** under `tests/milestoneN/` — with or without invoking `@execute-raise-defects` — the session **must** use a runner that produces:

1. **Local defect Excel** under `pipeline/test-data/MilestoneN/Defects/` (failures only)
2. **Execute-raise DOCX** under `docs/agent-runs/execute-raise-defects/`
3. **Summary JSON** at `results/qa-pipeline/defects/latest-module-run.json`

Google Sheet sync is **deferred** until the user approves the local workbook.

## Approved runners (use one — never bare Playwright alone)

| Command | When |
|---------|------|
| `npm run qa:run-module -- --spec <path>` | **Preferred** — headed, **1 worker**, one persistent Chromium (CDP); same window after failures |
| `npm run qa:execute-raise-defects -- --spec <path>` | Same as `qa:run-module` |
| `npm run milestone:run -- <N> <optional-path>` | Same persistent-browser behavior; auto-finalizes via pipeline reporter |

**Execution defaults (hard when user asks to run a module):**
- **Headed** — visible browser (`--headless` to opt out)
- **1 worker** — sequential (`--workers N` to override)
- **Persistent CDP Chromium** — one window for the full suite; Playwright worker restarts after failures reconnect to the same browser (`--no-persistent` to disable)
- Browser closes **only** when the run completes (or the runner exits)

Direct `npx playwright test tests/milestoneN/...` still auto-finalizes **if** the pipeline reporter runs and `PW_DEFER_DEFECT_GENERATION` / `PW_SKIP_MODULE_RUN_DOCX` are not set — but agents **must prefer** `qa:run-module` for explicit spec scope and Chromium ensure.

## Must not

- Run milestone specs with `PW_DEFER_DEFECT_GENERATION=1` unless a heal cycle owns defect timing (QA pipeline batch heal).
- Sync to Google during the initial run (no `--approve-google` / `PW_APPROVE_GOOGLE_DEFECT_SYNC=1` unless user explicitly approved in the same message).
- Skip DOCX because JSON artifacts exist.
- Hand-write defect rows — always `generateDefectFiles` / reporter + `finalize-module-run.cjs`.

## After run — tell the user

```
Local defect workbook: pipeline/test-data/MilestoneN/Defects/<module>-defects.xlsx
Agent run DOCX: docs/agent-runs/execute-raise-defects/<timestamp>_....docx

Reply **Approve defects** to sync to the Google Sheet Defects tab.
```

## Approval → Google sync

When the user replies `Approve defects` / `Approve Google` / equivalent:

```bash
npm run tracker:cdp-chrome   # if CDP Chrome not already running
npm run qa:approve-defects-sync
```

Or explicitly:

```bash
npm run qa:sync-defects-sheet -- \
  --rows results/qa-pipeline/defects/milestone-<N>-defect-rows.json \
  --approved
```

**Upsert + stale-row prune run by default** on approved sync (matches local Excel). Pass `--no-upsert` only to skip Google stale-module removal.

## Skip flags (internal only)

| Env | Effect |
|-----|--------|
| `PW_DEFER_DEFECT_GENERATION=1` | No defects/DOCX until post-heal finalize (QA pipeline) |
| `PW_SKIP_MODULE_RUN_DOCX=1` | Reporter skips DOCX; `execute-raise-defects` calls finalize once after run |
